boot: stzos init -- machine qemu_confine (hosted / x86_64 / qemu_pc) -- pid 1
boot: console /dev/ttyS0
boot: mount proc at /proc -- done
boot: mount sysfs at /sys -- done
boot: mount devtmpfs at /dev -- done
boot: mount tmpfs at /data -- done
boot: grant process (effectful)
boot: grant network (effectful)
boot: grant filesystem (effectful)
boot: network lan -- eth0 up 10.0.2.15/24, gateway 10.0.2.2 (dhcp), dns [10.0.2.3], /etc/resolv.conf written
boot: confine -- sealed has no network of its own, still has no sight of the other worlds and no way to start one, blind has no network of its own and no sight of /data; what a world did not declare, the kernel does not give it
boot: start sealed -- pid N -- /stzos confined eth0 /data
confined: eth0 -- no such interface from here: this world has a network namespace of its own and there is nothing in it
confined: processes -- this world is pid N and can see the machine's other processes: one table for everybody
confined: /data -- mounted here: this world can see the machine's storage
confined: fork -- permitted: this world started another process, and this line is the child speaking
boot: sealed (pid N) exited 0
boot: start still -- pid N -- /stzos confined eth0 /data
confined: eth0 -- present: this world shares the machine's network
confined: processes -- this world is pid 1 and no other process exists here: a table of its own
confined: /data -- mounted here: this world can see the machine's storage
confined: fork -- refused by the kernel (EPERM): this world cannot start another process
boot: still (pid N) exited 0
boot: start open -- pid N -- /stzos confined eth0 /data
confined: eth0 -- present: this world shares the machine's network
confined: processes -- this world is pid N and can see the machine's other processes: one table for everybody
confined: /data -- mounted here: this world can see the machine's storage
confined: fork -- permitted: this world started another process, and this line is the child speaking
boot: open (pid N) exited 0
boot: start blind -- pid N -- /stzos confined eth0 /data
confined: eth0 -- no such interface from here: this world has a network namespace of its own and there is nothing in it
confined: processes -- this world is pid N and can see the machine's other processes: one table for everybody
confined: /data -- an empty directory and nothing mounted on it: this world has a mount namespace of its own and the machine's storage is not in it
confined: fork -- permitted: this world started another process, and this line is the child speaking
boot: blind (pid N) exited 0
boot: judge -- the boot matches its expectation (/etc/expected, 19 lines)
boot: every service has ended -- init has nothing left to keep alive
boot: init halts the machine -- reboot(RESTART)
reboot: Restarting system
